// ============================================================
// MICRO:BIT CHESS
// Full engine — board representation, move generation, search,
// evaluation. Reflects every fix/addition made so far:
//   - bishop/rook/queen sliding-move generation fix
//   - search()/findBestMove() rewritten to fix the save/restore
//     corruption bug (global variables reused across recursion
//     levels of the same color parity)
//   - move ordering (captures/promotions first)
//   - quiescence search at the horizon
//   - time-budgeted iterative deepening (findBestMoveTimed)
//   - "attacking enemy pieces" evaluation sign fix
//   - castling heuristic: reward ACTUALLY castling, mildly
//     penalize losing castling rights without having castled
//
// No joystick or OLED yet. The built-in micro:bit display is
// used for simple testing via testGame().
//
// Board numbering:
// 0  1  2  3  4  5  6  7   = a8 ... h8
// 8  9 10 11 12 13 14 15   = a7 ... h7
// ...
// 56 57 58 59 60 61 62 63  = a1 ... h1
//
// Positive pieces = White, Negative pieces = Black
// 0 empty, 1 pawn, 2 knight, 3 bishop, 4 rook, 5 queen, 6 king
// ============================================================

