// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PER-PLY REUSABLE BUFFERS
//
// The search used to allocate brand-new move-list arrays and a brand-new
// board-copy array at EVERY node it visited -- tens of thousands of small
// arrays per move decision, which on a memory-constrained device like the
// micro:bit can exhaust or fragment the heap even though each one gets
// garbage collected (this was traced to the "020 / out of memory" panic).
// Since the search only ever has ONE node "active" at any given ply at a
// time (plain depth-first recursion, nothing concurrent), we only need
// ONE buffer PER PLY LEVEL, reused by every node that ever visits that
// ply, instead of one buffer per node. searchPly tracks how many real
// moves deep the current search line is (root = 0), and is the index
// into these pools. MAX_PLY is a hard safety cap -- normal play never
// gets remotely close to it, but it guarantees we can never index past
// the end of a pool array no matter how deep check extensions or
// quiescence captures chain together.
let MAX_PLY = 28
let searchPly = 0
let moveFromPool: number[][] = []
let moveToPool: number[][] = []
let movePromotionPool: number[][] = []
let moveCastlePool: number[][] = []
let moveEPPool: boolean[][] = []
