// Board data is stored FLAT (one 256-entry number[] covering all 4
// positions, 64 squares each) rather than as number[][] (an array of
// arrays). A nested array literal is untested on this compile target,
// and after two separate cases this project already hit of code that
// is completely valid TypeScript/JS but not supported by the actual
// on-device compiler (the .length setter; see historyTable's memory
// story above), a flat array using indexing we already know works
// everywhere else in this file is the safer bet over guessing that
